  "name": "Marie Rosier Wing",
  "status": "refined",
  "confidence": 0.46,
  "summary": "Two-storey L-shaped annex set behind Ursuline Hall, featuring a level roof, light buff walls, and a sheltered garden within the inside corner.",
  "style": "mid-century-modern",
  "evidence": [
    {
      "kind": "knowledge",
      "url": "https://tvsef.ca/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/brescia_map-TVSEF.pdf",
      "note": "The L-shaped wing directly west of Ursuline Hall is labelled Marie Rosier Wing."
    },
    {
      "kind": "knowledge",
      "url": "https://www.uwo.ca/fm/client_services/building_info.html",
      "note": "Western dates the Marie Rosier addition to 1971."
    },
    {
      "kind": "aerial",
      "note": "City of London 2025 orthophoto. L-shaped pale grey membrane, continuous coping, small vents and buff-coloured wall strips along the garden. Wall colour averaged on the visible garden-side face. Brick bond and opening dimensions are inferred."
    },
    {
      "kind": "kartaview",
      "frame": "146585449",
      "walls": [
        6
      ],
      "note": "The sightline to the wing is screened by Ursuline Hall. No openings can be counted from this approach."
    },
    {
      "kind": "lidar",
      "note": "Inventory P50 9.72 m, P90 9.82 m, maximum 10.34 m. Roof median 9.72 m and P90 9.82 m indicate a nearly constant parapet level."
    },
    {
      "kind": "aerial",
      "note": "A narrow lower roof meets the east end. Two wall projections face the garden and service side. The small circular objects and rectangular curb are distinguishable in the weathered membrane."
    },
    {
      "kind": "aerial",
      "note": "Marie Rosier Wing shows dark weathering concentrated over the west side and around the roof fittings, with pale concrete bordering the planted garden on two sides."
    }
  ],
